<h1>Justin Carmien</h1>
<p>48th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.just48.org/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (just48.org)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Running against Ald. Leni Manaa-Hoppenworth on what he calls &quot;progressivism 2.0,&quot; pursuing progressive goals through better-functioning government. His priorities include transit-oriented development around the new Red Line stations, housing stability through anti-displacement tools and an urban wealth fund approach to public assets, revitalized CAPS police meetings, and a Chicago city charter.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Communications designer at the Government Finance Officers Association; president of the Edgewater Beach Neighborhood Association since 2024. Moved to the 48th Ward in 2021.</p>
